#====================================================================
# Draft: Graphics/game-engine library with no native window backend on
#        OHOS — consume via the upstream headless compile mode
#        (compile-time macro, e.g. OLC_PGE_HEADLESS) instead of writing
#        a window backend / runtime dummy driver / test reclassification
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-OLCPIXELGAMEENGINE-2.30-OLC-PGE-HEADLESS-MODE
trigger_tool:           clang|conan_create|test_package|cmake
phase:                  compile|packaging|test_package
error_signature:        X11/X.h.*No such file|Xlib.h.*No such file|OLC_PLATFORM.*not defined|Package type is 'library', but no 'shared' option declared|no member named 'Resize' in 'olc::Sprite'

severity:               2
category:               ohos-graphics-headless-mode
match_keywords:         OLC_PGE_HEADLESS, OLC_PGE_APPLICATION, olcPixelGameEngine, single header,
                        game engine, headless, 无头, 无窗口后端, no display backend, header-only,
                        compile-time macro, consumer define, 消费方宏定义, package_type header-library

title:                  Single-header graphics/game-engine library with no native window backend on OHOS: use the upstream headless compile mode (OLC_PGE_HEADLESS) rather than writing a backend, runtime dummy drivers, or reclassifying display tests

root_cause:             The OHOS PC platform has no native windowing backend for windowed graphics engines (upstream olcPixelGameEngine covers only Win32/X11/GLUT/Emscripten). Compiling the header without a platform selection fails (missing X11 headers or no platform defined). Upstream DOES ship a real headless mode switched by a compile-time macro (OLC_PGE_HEADLESS -> OLC_PLATFORM_HEADLESS/OLC_GFX_HEADLESS/OLC_IMAGE_HEADLESS, upstream implementations, not stubs). The adaptation mistake is to write a new OHOS window backend, add runtime dummy drivers, or reclassify tests.

affected_scope:         Any windowed graphics / game-engine library (especially single-header C++17 ones) adapted to OHOS where upstream provides a headless/non-windowed compile mode; verified instance — olcPixelGameEngine 2.30 (OLC_PGE_HEADLESS).

verification_cmd:       clang++ -std=c++17 -O2 -fPIC -I<src> -pthread ohos_pge_test.cpp -o ohos_pge_test && ./ohos_pge_test   (headless: Sprite gradient fill/sample, headless Construct, vi2d ops, Pixel constants; exit 0)

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           use-upstream-headless-compile-mode-with-consumer-macro
rec_description:        Do not write a window backend, do not stub the platform, do not reclassify upstream tests. Prefer the upstream-supported headless/offscreen compile mode: the recipe must not patch the header; the consumer compiles with the headless macro defined (e.g. -DOLC_PGE_HEADLESS -DOLC_PGE_APPLICATION). Package header-only (package_type=header-library, copy headers into package_folder/include, no build artifact), validate with (1) a real consumer test in test_package that defines the macro and calls public APIs with observable results, and (2) a dedicated test_ohos case compiled directly with the OHOS toolchain running headless engine APIs. Report the 9 upstream missing-override warnings as upstream-fidelity noise.
rec_command:            target_compile_definitions(test PRIVATE OLC_PGE_HEADLESS OLC_PGE_APPLICATION); CXX_STANDARD 17; CONSUMER defines OLC_PGE_HEADLESS before OLC_PGE_APPLICATION before #include "olcPixelGameEngine.h"
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               none (source untouched; consumer-side macro only)

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      no-headless-mode-test-classification-and-probes
fallback_description:   If upstream has NO headless mode, follow E471 (classify display-dependent tests as failing suite, add no-display public-API probes as OHOS-specific tests) and E464/E472 (runtime dummy resource/driver patterns only where upstream documents them).
fallback_command:       meson test --no-suite=failing; add non-display API probe tests
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:

forbid_1_pattern:       #ifdef __OHOS__ platform macro in patches|stub platform returning OK without real logic|blanket -Wno-error|write a fake window backend
forbid_1_reason:        Patches with platform macros trip R8/PF5; headless mode is upstream-provided (real logic), while an invented stub backend is not; fake backends mask real capability gaps.
forbid_1_consequence:   Preflight rejection, non-portable patches, weakened downstream guarantees.

principles:             minimal-patch, upstream-fidelity, real-evidence-over-assumption, consumer-validation, ohos-platform-truth